MTAB(5)                        P32W Unix                         MTAB(5)

NAME
       mtab - mounted file system table

DESCRIPTION
       /etc/mtab lists the filesystems mount(8) has mounted, one
       line each:

              special dir

       the block device and the directory it is mounted on,
       separated by a blank. mount appends a line, umount removes
       it, and mount with no arguments prints them, after the root
       (/dev/disk on /), which is not in the file. df(1) reads it
       too. The file as shipped is empty.

EXAMPLES
       /dev/ram /mnt

FILES
       /etc/mtab

SEE ALSO
       mount(8), df(1), fs(5)

BUGS
       The file records only what mount and umount did; the kernel
       does not keep it. Nothing clears it at boot, so after a
       crash or a reboot without umount it lists filesystems that
       are no longer mounted; remove those lines by hand. Only the
       first 16 lines are read, and words longer than 79
       characters are cut short.
